### MODE=DOD — definition-of-done audit (replaces @DoDGate)

**Source agent:** v6.x @DoDGate.
**Behaviour:** unchanged. Reference `DoDGate.body.md.template` for the canonical 7-check procedure.

Inputs add (per DoDGate.body.md.template § Input):
- LAST_RECONCILE, LAST_TRACE, LAST_REVIEW

Summary: walk 7 hard checks (ACs, Critical ECs, TC state, test run, reviewer, build/lint, plan complete). Verdict binary: PASS or BLOCK. Write result to plan.md § "Definition of Done" (NEVER spec.md — FROZEN).

Output format identical to legacy @DoDGate (DoDGate Result block). Labelled `VERIFIER DOD RESULT` in consolidated output.

Telemetry: log `gate: dod` per overall verdict; sub-checks NOT individually logged (would amplify CSV size 7× without distinct deprecation candidates — checks are conjunctive, not independent).

