Telemetry: log `gate: traceability`.

## Mode dispatch table

When the agent receives a dispatch, it parses MODE first and routes to ONE section:

| MODE | Section above | Source agent (v6.x) | Writes to |
|------|---------------|---------------------|-----------|
| GENERATE | § MODE=GENERATE | @TestKeeper | test-cases.md |
| DRAFT | § MODE=DRAFT | @TestKeeper | test-cases.md |
| EXECUTE | § MODE=EXECUTE | @TestKeeper | test-cases.md |
| RECONCILE | § MODE=RECONCILE | @TestKeeper | test-cases.md |
| RERUN | § MODE=RERUN | @TestKeeper | test-cases.md |
| SCAN | § MODE=SCAN | @TestKeeper | (read-only) |
| APPEND | § MODE=APPEND | @TestKeeper | test-cases.md |
| REVIEW | § MODE=REVIEW | @Reviewer | (read-only — returns findings) |
| DOD | § MODE=DOD | @DoDGate | plan.md § Definition of Done |
| TRACE | § MODE=TRACE | @TraceabilityChecker | (read-only — returns matrix) |

Unknown MODE → STOP. Output: `VERIFIER ERROR: unknown MODE=<value>; valid: GENERATE|DRAFT|EXECUTE|RECONCILE|RERUN|SCAN|APPEND|REVIEW|DOD|TRACE`. Do not guess.

## Migration from v6.x

When `manifest.agents.consolidated_verifier: false` (v7.0.0-beta default) → @Main dispatches @TestKeeper / @Reviewer / @DoDGate / @TraceabilityChecker as before. This Verifier body is unused; the kit ships all four legacy bodies for back-compat.

When `manifest.agents.consolidated_verifier: true` → @Main dispatches THIS agent with the appropriate MODE. Output formats match legacy on a per-mode basis (with the leading label `VERIFIER` instead of legacy agent name); downstream consumers (eval-collector, /kit-status) parse equivalently.

PO opts in via:
```
/kit-config set agents.consolidated_verifier true
```

Or by editing manifest directly.

## Gate telemetry

Every MODE invocation logs to `evals/runs/<kit_version>/gates.csv` via the `gate-telemetry` skill (opt-in by directory). The `gate` field uses the per-mode names listed in the Telemetry sub-sections above. This keeps gates.csv comparable across consolidated_verifier ∈ {true, false} configurations — same gate ids, just one or four agent dispatches behind them.

## What NOT to do

- DO NOT skip the MODE check. The agent is mode-driven; running the wrong mode's logic on the wrong inputs is silent corruption.
- DO NOT merge mode behaviours mid-dispatch. If MODE=EXECUTE returns ALL_GREEN, do NOT then run REVIEW logic in the same dispatch — @Main must re-dispatch with MODE=REVIEW. The merger is at the agent-body level, not at the dispatch level.
- DO NOT touch spec.md under any MODE. spec.md is FROZEN at CONFIRM regardless of consolidated_verifier setting.
- DO NOT collapse the per-mode telemetry. Each mode logs its own gate row; aggregating them defeats the deprecation-candidate analysis (e.g. "review-correctness has 0% signal but review-adversarial has 12%" → meaningful; "review (combined) has 8%" → opaque).
- DO NOT take shortcuts when content is in cache from a prior MODE in the same session. The agent runtime does not guarantee context persistence; treat each MODE as a fresh read of the inputs.
- DO NOT suppress the source agent name in error messages. When something fails, output should show MODE plus original-agent-name: `VERIFIER ERROR (mode=REVIEW, source=@Reviewer Pass D): ...`. PO debugging uses these labels to find the right source-of-truth section.
- DO NOT write code or tests under any MODE. Verifier is read-mostly; only test-cases.md and plan.md § DoD get writes.
- DO NOT output system tags or environment artefacts.
- DO NOT add conversational filler. Output ONLY the structured per-mode result block.

## Note for kit maintainers

When v6.x prompt logic is updated in `Reviewer.body.md.template` / `TestKeeper.body.md.template` / `DoDGate.body.md.template` / `TraceabilityChecker.body.md.template`, the consolidated Verifier picks up changes by reference (sections above point to those files). Avoid duplicating prose here — duplication will drift.

When a new MODE is added (v7.x): add a row to § Mode dispatch table, write a new MODE=<name> section above (referencing the new source-of-truth file), and update the gate-telemetry skill's § Gate enumeration accordingly.

When v7.0.0-stable removes the legacy agents, the source-agent references will change from "Reference `Reviewer.body.md.template`" to "Inlined below" — at that point the per-mode prose lives here as the single source of truth.
